  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid VMAT2 criteria, effective 2025-11-01. Austedo / Austedo XR (deutetrabenazine) and Ingrezza (valbenazine) share adult HD chorea and moderate\u2013severe TD paths. Xenazine (tetrabenazine) is HD chorea only, with two distinct generic manufacturers tried and failed. Clinical rationale, specialty consultation, scores and trial/failure evidence require manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): Restlessness, agitation, akathisia and parkinsonism: reduce dose or discontinue if occurs. Sedation/somnolence may impair driving or operating machinery. QTc prolongation: combination with other QTc-prolonging drugs is not recommended.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial 3 months; reauthorization 12 months with documented marked improvement in functional impairment, defined as \u22652-point improvement from baseline on at least one AIMS line 1\u20137 with baseline line-item score \u22653. Renewal requires manual review.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 34-day supply. Austedo: 6 mg 2 tablets/day; 9 mg and 12 mg 4 tablets/day. Austedo XR: 6, 12, 18, 30, 36, 42 and 48 mg 1 tablet/day; 24 mg 2 tablets/day. Ingrezza: 40, 60 and 80 mg 1 capsule/day. Xenazine: 12.5 and 25 mg 4 tablets/day. Product-specific quantity, duration and cautions require manual review; max_units is null. PDL status unknown; no linked alternatives."
  ],
